Task 7 - Determine if IOP is applicable

An entitlement for Interest on Overpayment (IOP) is applicable if the following conditions are met:

taxpayer initiates GIC remission request in relation to a GIC amount that has been paid 

the refund that arises from the remission is issued more than 30 days from the day on which the request was made, and

the auto GIC is in respect of the period before 01/07/2010, with an effective date on or before 01/07/2010.

Warning
If the remission is relating to manual GIC, further investigation is required as the manual GIC amount could include GIC for the period before and after 01/07/2010.

IOP is not applicable on:

system automated GIC remission amounts
ATO initiated remissions
credit GIC amendment from the processing of a form
Client initiated GIC remission requests where the refund is issued within 30 days from which the request is made
any auto GIC in respect of the period after 30/06/2010, with an effective date after 01/07/2010.
Information

