How to escalate taxpayer enquiries as a result of activity statement refunds being held in a frozen bank account.

Last published 18 August 2025

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

This page instructs staff on how to escalate taxpayer enquiries as a result of activity statement refunds or Income Tax being held in a frozen bank account.

Taxpayers may call the ATO advising their bank or financial institution has frozen their account. This may be due to a suspect ATO refund being paid into their account.

The ATO:

and several financial institutions have noticed an increase in the number of ATO tax refund payments needing further review
is working closely with banks and is undertaking reviews to confirm if the ATO refund has been paid into the correct account.
Operation Protego Siebel Alert

Siebel Alert 'Operation Protego' was created to assist in recognising taxpayers who were identified as potentially high risk due to claims relating to fraudulent GST refunds. These Alerts are no longer being added to taxpayer accounts from 30 June 2023.

Do not remove any suppressions or take any action in relation to any possible refunds or remediation.

To avoid risks that may arise from identifying case officers, only disclose:

their first name, and
contact number (as shown on the outcome letter).

Do not disclose the case officer's full name.

