What happens next?  

If your report involves a case that you are working on, you must continue working on your case while FCB is conducting an assessment for a potential criminal investigation or other responses (unless you are otherwise advised by FCB). Continuing the case may include actions such as remediation, adjustments, debt collection and consideration of a referral to the TPB where appropriate.

The Criminal Law Program in FCB will work with your business area or the relevant External Fraud Sub-Risk Owner in relation to risk prioritisation and subsequent resourcing decisions.

Reports not suitable for investigation and prosecution will still be captured for reporting and intelligence purposes.

Reporting suspicion of external fraud assists to:

improve intelligence on external fraud
understand the risk environment
monitor the level of suspected fraud against the system
inform the Audit and Risk Committee on the level of fraud in the system.

