Procedure Steps
Before you begin

A refund can be generated in two ways from ICP without the processing of a form:

automatic credit balance processing based on ICP business rules

manual credit balance processing initiated by ATO staff.

Where a credit balance request (CBR) is processed, ICP will generate a number of automated request transactions. Each request transaction represents an item of correspondence that potentially will be issued to the taxpayer. If these Request transactions are cancelled before the nightly batch processes are run at approximately 5pm Canberra time, then no correspondence will be created. Once batch processing occurs, accounting processes and correspondence will need to be manually reversed to effect the cancellation.

To complete a refund cancellation you will require ICP access to:

view and modify request transactions
input debit and credit suppressions
cancel penalty and interest
cancel credit transfers and internal offsets.
