In Detail
Higher than expected

If a taxpayer advises they have received a larger refund than expected or requested, they may have had a credit on their account which was included in their refund.

Where a small credit balance exists on the taxpayer's activity statement account (currently amounts less than $100), this amount will now be included and issued when an activity statement is processed for refunding at the same time.

The existing small credit will be available for offsetting to other debts the taxpayer may have. Delayed refund interest (DRI), although payable on the activity statement credit, will not be calculated on this additional amount.

A note will be added to the taxpayer's file, however no additional correspondence will be sent to the taxpayer.

If a taxpayer advises their refund amount is incorrect and it does not fall under the above scenario, escalate the enquiry to Accounting, depending on the account type.

Lower than expected

If the refund the taxpayer received matches the amount showing on their account, they may just require an account explanation (for example the taxpayer may have had a debt outstanding on their account which was offset using the credit, then the balance was refunded).

