Procedure to action company HRR review items.

Last published 15 April 2026

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

This page provides the procedure to action company High Risk Refund (HRR) review items.

The ICP system generates a HRR review item and associated Siebel activity when a refund meets the criteria for one or more HRR rules. These rules run as part of credit balance request (CBR).

Information

CBR runs whenever there is a credit balance requires issuing. This occurs even if a form has not been lodged. Each time CBR runs, it calls on the Credit Risk Assessment module and applies HRR rules.

After the CBR has run, all activities are passed through the HRR automation model with low-risk items closed and the remainder routed for manual action. For manual items, the activity description is updated to include rules that failed.

Forms lodged pre 2012 have passed through the automation model however cannot be validated and need manual intervention by HRR operatives. A full review will be needed for these activities. The activities will be classified as:

Capability: ICP Maintain Account

Category: Risk Item

Type: Companies

Interaction: ICP Update.

