Procedure Steps
Activity reallocation policy
What is reallocation

Reallocation is the process to move an activity from one in-tray to another in-tray in Siebel.

If you are unable to action an activity or a group of activities, you can reallocate them to a suitable:

tax officer
team in-tray, or
ENTERPRISE_Q.

Note: Use the escalation flag when first reallocating activities with the following interactions:

Inbound Phone
IVR Self Help
Web Chat, or
Shopfront.

Activities with these interactions are not covered in this policy. For more information refer to Escalation - non phone escalation policy.
Opens in a new window

An activity may need to be reallocated when:

it cannot be completed within service standard by the team or individual, due to planned or unplanned leave
the receiving officer cannot action the activity as they do not have the required knowledge or skills
it has been incorrectly allocated to a team or individual in-tray
it has been split and the extra activities need to be actioned by a different team or individual
there is a change in business work priorities, or
actions to be taken by another user as part of case work.
Information

Team Leaders can reallocate activities using the same steps. They have more functionality to enable the reallocation of multiple activities at once. This is by using the Change Records function.

Refer to Update activity - change records in Siebel
Opens in a new window
 for the steps on how to perform this task in Siebel.

Before reallocating an activity, complete the following actions where required:

reclassify the activity
work out the correct in-tray to receive the activity, and
seek approval from your team leader if reallocating an activity to another team within your functional area.
Reallocation rules

There are enterprise rules that must be followed when reallocating an activity.

Activities may be reallocated:

to anyone within the same team, as per agreed team work practices
to another team in-tray
within the same functional area
by a team leader (or under instruction from a team leader), or
outside a functional area, through the Enterprise Capture Processing Unit.
Reallocate due to planned leave

Before taking planned leave, you should:

view My Activities in-tray, and
check if any activities will need action during your leave period.
Information

Consider any activities that:

have a high Priority status, or
are approaching their due date.

Before reallocating an activity:

consult your team leader to identify a member in your team that has capacity to receive these activities
notify the team member that they will be receiving more activities
keep the Status of the activity as In Progress when reallocating to someone in your team.
Reallocate due to unplanned leave

When a team member is away due to unplanned leave, a team leader should:

log onto Siebel, and
run a query to check if the team member has any active activities in their in-tray.

The team leader should:

review the team members active activities, and
check if any need reallocation. To check this, consideration should be given to the activity Due Date and Status.
Information

Only a team leader has access to view and update activities that are allocated to a member of their team.

Team leaders may need to reallocate activities to meet service standards.
Opens in a new window

Before reallocating, the team leader needs to:

identify a member of their team who has the capacity to receive the extra activities
consult the receiving team member about the reallocation of the activities, and
keep the Status of the activity as In Progress when reallocating to someone in the team.
Reallocate as outside skills, knowledge or delegation

You may not be able to action an activity that you receive or create due to not having the required:

skills
knowledge
delegations.

This may occur when:

you receive extra linked activities (by Service Requests) but cannot action them due to not having the required skills or knowledge
an activity has been incorrectly classified. Once it has been reclassified, it needs to be actioned by another team or functional area
an original activity has been split into separate activities. Once the activities are classified, they need to be actioned by a different team or functional area.

Use the correct classification when reallocating the activity outside of your functional area. If unsure of the correct classification, update the Type field to Unclassified before reallocating to ENTERPRISE_Q. Enterprise Capture Processing will then work out the correct classification.

When reallocating the activities to a team in-tray, the activity Status must be updated to UnAllocated.

Participants

A participant is a tax officer that has been added to the Assigned To field of the activity. This allows the participant to view the activity in their in-tray.

An activity can have one or more participants. Where there is more than one participant for the activity, a primary owner should be nominated.

The primary owner is:

the tax officer who has the responsibility for ensuring that all the required actions have been undertaken to complete the activity
indicated by placing a 'tick' in the Primary field in the Employees dialog box. This is available by selecting the MVG in the Assigned To field.
Taking ownership of an activity

There may be instances where you need to take ownership of an activity. Some instances are:

a business process advises you to
it is initiated by taxpayer contact, or
you are actioning a related activity.
Warning

The activity may already be assigned to another operative. Work out if it is suitable for you to take ownership of the activity by having a discussion with:

the other operative, or
your Team Leader.

Go to How to take ownership of an activity when you:

need to take ownership of an activity, and
have selected the Activity Id hyperlink to open the activity Details view.
