How to remit sundry manual general interest charge (GIC) transactions in ICP.

Last published 28 April 2026

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

How to remit sundry manual general interest charge (GIC) transactions in ICP.

In ICP manual GIC is applied using sundry transactions with appropriate input reasons. To remit sundry manual GIC, you add a new sundry transaction with an appropriate input reason for the manual GIC remission type.

Limited system validations

This applies for sundry transactions.

Warning

Care must be taken with the following listed below.

Manual GIC details are accurate.
The transaction is applied to the correct role and period.
You do not remit more than the value of the original sundry manual GIC transaction.
Remission amount does not include auto GIC.

In limited circumstances, debit sundry manual GIC remission adjustment transaction can be used to reverse an incorrect GIC remission. The debit sundry must have the same effective date as the incorrect GIC remission that you are reversing. Refer to procedure Update - Correct over remission of penalty, cost or fine.
Opens in a new window

Warning

Do not remit the amount of GIC subject to non-pursuit/release without re-raising the debt. The non-pursuit must be re-raised to absorb the GIC credits. If you are unsure, consult your coach.

