How to check for an external collection agency (ECA) referral in Siebel.

Last published 31 January 2025

Favourite Notes Collapse all 
Background

The ECA commenced actioning ATO referrals from 5th February 2024.

This page explains how to check for an external collection agency (ECA) referral in Siebel.

Recent updates
13/05/2024	

Multiple updates made across the page.

	SD-80910
Procedure Steps
Confirm ECA referral

Confirm if a case has been referred to an ECA by checking either of the following:

Taxpayer Indicator in ECP
Client Consolidated View (CCV) in Siebel
Case Summary in Siebel.
ECP Taxpayer Indicator

Go to ECP:

select the Taxpayer tab
review the Taxpayer Indicator gadget for the External Collection Agency.
If the case is...	Then the indicator field will display a...
referred	Y
not referred
	N

Retrieval may take up to 14 days to update in our system. If the taxpayer believes they have been withdrawn and the indicator is Y, check CCV.

Taxpayer Consolidated View

Go to CCV in Siebel.

Select the Query, then Go. This will show all internal activities that may not have previously been visible.

Look for a Siebel activity with following classifications:

Capability: Debt Case
Category: Collection negotiation
Type: Referred to mercantile agent 2
Interaction: Internal - case for routing.

If the above activity is:

found and the status is
UnAllocated, the case has been referred and still remains with the ECA
Not applicable or Done,
the case has been retrieved from the ECA
continue with the next appropriate action using existing procedures. This is the end of the procedure

not found, check Case Summary.

Case Summary

Go to the Case summary tab.

Check for an active debt case with the following criteria:

Status: On Hold
Sub Status: Referral
Project: Referred to Mercantile Agent.

Open the case activity Id:

go to the Details tab
review the
External reference ID fields
External reference type fields.
