Payment plan - Approve

The period of any payment plan is calculated from the decision date.

The amount is based on the total amount of all tax-related liabilities subject to the decision.

If the amount across all accounts for the entity is above your authorisation, the entire request must be escalated to the appropriate level. This includes debts in an active payment arrangement.

For example, you must not activate an:

arrangement on one account and then seek approval to activate an arrangement for the remaining debt on another account when the combined debt exceeds your authorisation, or
interim arrangement, regardless of the instalment amounts, without seeking approval where total outstanding account balances exceeds your authorisation.
